    <p class="blog-article-lede">The original post has been removed because I cannot support its first-person engineering narrative, model/hardware details, performance figures, or quality claims with reproducible artifacts.</p>
    <div class="blog-body">
      <h2>Why it was withdrawn</h2>
      <p>The article was drafted with AI assistance and presented a polished story as established fact. The repository does not contain the exact model artifact, quantization, commands, patches, raw logs, benchmark method, or result files needed to audit those claims. Leaving it published would ask readers to trust a story I cannot presently substantiate.</p>
      <h2>What would be required to republish it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Exact public model identifiers, revisions, hashes, and quantization details.</li>
        <li>Hardware, operating-system, runtime, build, and storage configuration.</li>
        <li>Commands, code changes, raw logs, prompts, outputs, and repeatable timing methodology.</li>
        <li>A clear split between measured results, observations, and projections.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Until that evidence exists, there is no technical claim here to rely on. The withdrawal is the honest version.</p>
